-- check/bad: `(==)` and friends are a lambda over a method call
-- (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §3.1, Appendix A.22), and §1.3
-- promises that every message about a well-known call names the OPERATOR.
-- So an arity or type mistake on one says "The (==) operator", not "This
-- value": too_few_args at 10:6, too_many_args at 15:6, type_mismatch at
-- 20:9. The hand-written lambda at the bottom is the control — it is not
-- an operator section and must not be named as one (too_few_args at 25:5).
--
-- `wrongType` compares a `String` with an `Int` and not a `String` with a
-- `String`: on this branch `<` is the receiver's `compare` method (§3.1) and
-- `"a" < "b"` COMPILES, so the mistake has to be one the operator's own
-- pinning rule catches — both operands are one type (A.33).
pub tooFew : Int -> Bool
tooFew n = (==) n


pub tooMany : Bool
tooMany = (<) 1 2 3


pub wrongType : Bool
wrongType = (<) "a" 1


pub handWritten : Int -> Bool
handWritten n = (\a b -> a == b) n
